WOW-BG3 benilla patch 0096: indoors, the see-through takes the terrain too.

In a cave the camera is not bumped (0095), so it often sits behind the hill the cave lies in, and terrain
was never cut: the character stood behind a piece of mountain and a click on the floor landed on it. While
she is indoors the capsule now cuts terrain as it does everything else, with the same floor rule (nothing
under 0.35 yd over her feet). Outdoors nothing changes. The plugin's cursor goes through the same terrain.

diff --git a/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_see.rs b/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_see.rs
--- a/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_see.rs
+++ b/crates/benilla-app/src/wowbg3_see.rs
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@
         near: s.near.max(0.0),
         noise_amp: s.amp.max(0.0),
         noise_scale: s.scale,
-        terrain: s.terrain,
+        terrain: s.terrain || crate::wowbg3_lead::she_is_indoors(),
         phase: s.phase,
         ..SeeThrough::default()
     };
